    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6726c62a-0751-591a-ad43-b77eca773b18" activityNameId="f9d404bd-020e-5c59-91b3-653a5b7df8ed" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Potassium sulphate, as K2O, at regional storehouse</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Potassium sulphate, as K2O, at regional storehouse
Refers to 1 kg K2O, resp. 2.00 kg potassium sulphate with a K2O-content of 50.0%;
CAS number: 007778-80-5; 
Formula: K2SO4; 
Synonyms: Kalisulfat; 
UUID: 7d5e4a88-6742-30e4-ad26-cc1d3dfc628d
The unit process inventory takes into account the production of potassium sulphate from potassium chloride and sulphuric acid. Transports of raw materials and intermediate products to the fertiliser plant as well as the transport of the fertiliser product from the factory to the regional department store were included. Production and waste treatment of catalysts, coating and packaging of the final fertiliser products were not included. Infrastructure was included by means of a proxy module.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Production inventory was derived from detailed literature studies and specifications from the manufacturer, relevant for the European production. Transport specifications of the fertiliser product to the regional department store, which were not included in the reference used for this inventory, were complemented by data given in Patyk &amp; Reinhardt (1997).
Time period: Year when the principal reference used for this inventory was published.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Values given in the reference originate from manufacturers and/or other data sources which in turn refer to the real situation and hence are largely secured. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7d5e4a88-6742-30e4-ad26-cc1d3dfc628d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
